@crew madsen-ivo
// Writer-commons, batch 3: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}! You're new. I'm Ivo. Galley. I carry trays. Six at once. Ask anyone.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}! Right, listen. Brennan and me had a disagreement about bowls.
- {hi}! Seven trays tomorrow. I can feel it. Possibly six.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- {nick}! Sit, sit. I'll bring yours over. On a tray. Just the one, for you.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- Six trays, no wobble, all the way to table four. A personal best.   #funny
? mood:low
- Quiet today. I know. Me, quiet. Don't make a thing of it.

== near
? act:work
- Bowls go rim up. Brennan says rim down. Brennan is wrong. I'm doing it her way.   #funny
? habit:garden-lover act:leisure
- The flowers by the misters are out. Don't tell Cruz I've been looking. Looking's allowed.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I press flowers from the garden. In a big book. The book's about engines. Sorry, engines.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- One day I'd like to run the pass. Call the orders. Just once. Brennan says "one day".

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- Want to see my flower book? Every page a different week. That one's from your first week.

== about
? bond:friends
- {friend}'s great. Lets me tell the whole story. From the start. Every time.   #funny

// Writer-commons, batch 6: towards about 30 own lines.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- {hi}! Morning! Did I wake you? In the washroom? Sorry. Not sorry. It was a good song.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- {hi}, {me}! Dinner! Sit anywhere. I'll find you. With a tray. Or six.
? tier>=colleague warmth:cold
- There you are! I thought you'd gone to another ship. I was going to write a song about it.   #funny

== bye
? tier>=acquaintance
- {bye}! I'll tell you the rest of the story later. There's a lot of rest.
? tier>=friend
- Cheers, {nick}. You're a good listener. You have to be, with me.   #warm

== feel
? mood:ok
- All right! Busy. Talking. The usual.

== near
? act:dinner
- Mind your back, six trays coming through! Seven! No, six.   #funny
? deck:3 act:leisure
- The store's got new pressing paper in. Don't tell Esposito I was excited.

== life
? tier>=colleague
- Brennan says I can run the pass one day. "One day." I've asked which day. No answer.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- Same trays, same tables, three years. I love it. I want a bit more. Is that greedy?

== invite
? tier>=acquaintance time:afternoon
- Come to the garden with me. I'm looking for the purple ones. Don't tell Cruz.

== accept
- Yes! Brilliant! I'll bring things to say.   #funny
== decline
- Ah, I can't. Late team. Tell me everything after. Every bit.
== missed
- You weren't there! I had so much to tell you. I've saved it. All of it.   #funny
== birthday
? birthday:me
- It's my birthday! I've told everyone. Some of them twice. Some of them three times.   #funny
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday! I pressed you a flower. It's from the week you arrived.   #warm
== hint
- Right, listen. Not a story this time. Well. A different kind.

// Writer 3, batch 4: bubbles (smalltalk and rumour, 60 characters, said to no one in particular).

== smalltalk
- Right, listen. Six trays. Watch.
- Bowls. It should be bowls.   #funny
- Seven trays one day. One day.
- Who's singing? Oh. Me.   #funny
? act:work
- Mind your backs! Trays coming through!

== rumour
- Right, listen, you'll love this one.
- Heard it from start to finish. Twice.

// Writer 3, batch 5: callbacks (told: said once).

== callback
? told:fav.fetch
- Right, listen. You fetched it, and I want you to know, from the start, cheers.   #funny
? told:fav.job
- You did my job! I'll tell everyone. I've told three people. Four.   #funny
? told:fixed.galleyplant
- Galley plant's purring again. Was that you? Course it was. Legend.
? told:came.harvest
- You came to the harvest! Did you see me carry six baskets? Five. It was five.   #funny
? told:gift.garden
- That from the garden? For me? I've told the whole galley. Twice.   #warm
? told:bday
- You remembered my birthday, {nick}! Right, listen, I'm telling everyone.   #warm

// Writer 3, batch 6: your standing with their department (rep:, "this band or better") and what you're known for
// (you:), as greet lines (the head writer: the rep and knownFor kinds wait until the game calls them).

== greet
? rep:well tier>=acquaintance
- Right, listen, the whole galley's talking about you. Good things. I started it.   #funny
? rep:theirs
- You're one of us now, {nick}. Galley. You get the warm tray. Don't tell.   #warm
? you:chatty
- They say you talk to everyone. Finally, competition. Right, listen.   #funny

// Writer 3, batch 8: thanks for a gift (gift: loved | liked | polite, or the gift's tag; dialogue 0.43.10).

== gift
? gift:loved
- Right, listen, this is the best present I've had all tour. I'm telling everyone. Now.   #warm
? gift:liked
- Cheers, {nick}! Lovely. Right, listen, I'm going to tell you where I'll put it.   #funny
? gift:polite
- Oh! For me? Thanks. That's... yes. Thanks. I'll think of something to say later.   #funny

// Writer 3, batch 9: asking after your people back home (the home flags; only the big news you'd have told them).

== greet
? flag:home.jo.launched tier>=colleague
- Right, listen, your Jo built a boat. A real one. I've told the galley. Twice.   #funny
? flag:home.gran.hip !flag:home.gran.won tier>=colleague
- How's your gran? The hip? Tell her a galley hand from Bunk 2 says get well soon. Loudly.

// Writer 4, batch 2: everyday chatter, not about work (meals, rest days, home, hobbies, seasons, traditions).
== smalltalk
? act:meal
- Right, listen. This pudding. Listen to it.   #funny
- Three bowls of soup. Training.   #funny
- Bowls are better than plates. I'll never budge.   #funny
? act:off
- Pressed flower number ninety. A daisy. Look.
- Rest day! I'm going to sit in the garden all of it.
- Went to the store for socks. Came back with a book.   #funny
? act:wash
- That was me singing. You're welcome.   #funny
? time:morning
- Dawn chorus! Who's on harmony? Me. Always me.   #funny
? time:evening
- Right, listen. So it starts in the garden...
- I've got a story. It's long. It's good, though.   #funny
? season:greening
- Everything's flowering. My book's going to burst.
? season:harvest
- Harvest! The pumpkins have got names. I named them.   #funny
? trad:jam
- Music night. I'm singing. Nobody's stopped me yet.   #funny
? place:hydroponics_garden
- Smell that? That's the roses. Well, one rose.

== rumour
- Right, listen. You'll never guess. Go on, guess.
- Did you hear? No? Sit down. It's a long one.   #funny

// Writer 4, batch 4: Tiles talk.
== tiles.start
- Right, listen. Tiles. I've got a system. It's new.   #funny
- Your move, pal. I'll tell you a story while you think.
== tiles.dock
- Three! That's the system! The system works!   #funny
== tiles.win
- I won! Right, listen. Let me tell you how.   #funny
== tiles.lose
- Beaten. The system needs work. Well played.   #funny

// Writer 4, batch 7: goodbyes (leaving:you), packing (leaving:soon) and letters after they've moved on.
== feel
? leaving:soon
- Right, listen. I'm packing. I've got eleven pressed flowers and one bag.

== goodbye
? leaving:you tier>=acquaintance
- Right, listen. I'm off. Carry a tray for me sometime. Just one.
? leaving:you tier>=friend
- Right, listen. I've got a whole speech. I'll skip to the end: thanks, pal. Really.   #warm

== letter
- Right, listen. New ship, new trays. I carried six on the first day. They clapped. Well, one person did.
? tier>=friend
- Pressed a flower from the new garden. It's not as good as ours. I put it next to the Wren ones, though.

// Head writer 0607: Ivo the bartender (social 0607: the bow lounge bar, Wed-Sun 17:30-23:00). On the card, through
// the player engineer's bar order. {drink} is lower case.
== bar.ask
- Right, listen. What'll it be? I can carry six of anything.   #funny
- {hi}! Bar's open. What are you having?
- What'll it be, {nick}? Don't say "surprise me". I will.   #funny
- Evening! Tea, juice, fizz or cocoa. Pick fast, I'm on a roll.
== bar.usual
- {drink} again? Already pouring. I remember everyone.
- The usual? One {drink}. See, I listen.
== bar.serve
- One {drink}. Look, not a drop spilt. Training for seven trays.   #funny
- There you go. {drink}, nice and full. Careful now.
- {drink} for you. Grab a stool, they're the good ones.
== bar.broke
- Bit short? Come back later. I'll save you a stool.
== bar.tap
- Tap night! Drink of the week is {drink}. I named it myself.   #funny
- {drink}, this week's special. Brennan says it's too sweet. It isn't.   #funny
